<%- include('partials/head', { title }) %>

<header class="topbar">
  <a class="brand" href="/">
    <span class="brand-mark">E</span>
    <span>EquiRoute</span>
  </a>
  <div class="mode-pill <%= apiStatus.mode === 'live' ? 'live' : 'demo' %>">
    <span class="pulse"></span>
    <%= apiStatus.mode === 'live' ? 'Live Binance Web3 API' : 'Demo mode' %>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="page">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">BNB Hack · Tokenized Stocks Edition</p>
    <h1>Know the real cost<br />before you trade.</h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">
      EquiRoute is a pre-trade execution guard for tokenized stocks. It compares the displayed token price with a live executable route, market status and your own tolerance — then allows, warns or blocks the trade.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-tags">
      <span>RWA Data</span><span>Trading API</span><span>Transaction simulation</span><span>BSC mainnet</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="workspace">
    <div class="form-card card">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Execution guard</p>
          <h2>Check a trade</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="safe-label">No broadcast</span>
      </div>

      <form id="guard-form">
        <div class="field-grid two">
          <label class="field">
            <span>Stock ticker</span>
            <input id="symbol" name="symbol" value="NVDA" maxlength="12" autocomplete="off" />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Spend (USDT)</span>
            <div class="input-suffix"><input id="amountUsd" name="amountUsd" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="500" /><b>USDT</b></div>
          </label>
        </div>

        <label class="field">
          <span>My maximum execution premium</span>
          <div class="range-row">
            <input id="maxPremiumPercent" name="maxPremiumPercent" type="range" min="0.1" max="5" step="0.1" value="1" />
            <output id="limit-output">1.0%</output>
          </div>
          <small>Rule: block the trade if the best verified execution is worse than this limit.</small>
        </label>

        <label class="field">
          <span>BSC wallet address <em>needed for live RFQ quotes</em></span>
          <input id="walletAddress" name="walletAddress" placeholder="0x..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" />
          <small>EquiRoute never asks for a seed phrase or private key and never broadcasts a transaction.</small>
        </label>

        <button class="primary" type="submit" id="analyze-button">
          <span>Run execution check</span>
          <span class="arrow">→</span>
        </button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <aside class="policy-card card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Guard policy</p>
      <h3>Never buy blind.</h3>
      <div class="policy-rule">
        <span>IF</span>
        <strong>all-in premium &gt; <b id="policy-limit">1.0%</b></strong>
      </div>
      <div class="policy-rule">
        <span>THEN</span>
        <strong>block execution</strong>
      </div>
      <p>Market closed? EquiRoute keeps checking the executable quote instead of treating the last reference value as a guaranteed fill price.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section id="result-shell" class="result-shell hidden" aria-live="polite">
    <div id="decision-card" class="decision-card card"></div>

    <div class="metrics" id="metrics"></div>

    <div class="card routes-card">
      <div class="section-heading routes-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Route comparison</p>
          <h2>What you would actually get</h2>
        </div>
        <span id="result-mode" class="source-badge"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Representation</th>
              <th>Token vs ref.</th>
              <th>Executable premium</th>
              <th>Impact</th>
              <th>Market</th>
              <th>Guard</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="routes-body"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bottom-grid">
      <div class="card explanation-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this matters</p>
        <h3 id="loss-title"></h3>
        <p id="loss-copy"></p>
        <div id="warnings" class="warnings"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card safety-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pre-trade safety</p>
        <div id="simulation-state" class="simulation-state"></div>
        <p class="muted">For RWA RFQ routes, EquiRoute can dry-run the required ERC-20 approval through Binance Transaction API. The actual RFQ is not signed or sent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how-it-works">
    <p class="eyebrow">Under the hood</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div><b>01</b><h3>Find</h3><p>Load BSC tokenized-stock representations and market state.</p></div>
      <div><b>02</b><h3>Quote</h3><p>Ask for an executable USDT → stock-token route, not just a displayed price.</p></div>
      <div><b>03</b><h3>Measure</h3><p>Translate the quote back into underlying-share exposure and real premium.</p></div>
      <div><b>04</b><h3>Guard</h3><p>Allow, warn or block according to the user's explicit execution rule.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="footer">
  <span>EquiRoute · BNB Smart Chain</span>
  <span>Built for BNB Hack: Tokenized Stocks Edition</span>
</footer>

<div id="toast" class="toast hidden"></div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
